{
  "version": 2,
  "engine": "micro",
  "name": "micro_ortho_field",
  "description": "Ortho field: a fixed 1 kHz sine turned halfway toward stepped noise, a grain of held values around the tone that clicks at a steady rate, cut by a gate on the sixteenth; a breathing low pole under it. Macro 1 moves the amount, from the sine to noise.",
